# This checkout lives on a drive shared with Windows, and something on that side
# rewrites files with CRLF line endings. Git stored LF, so every one of those
# files showed as modified: 299 files, 741,851 insertions and 741,851 deletions,
# with `git diff --ignore-all-space` completely empty — not one byte of real
# change. That made `git add -A` a trap (any real commit would be buried under
# three-quarters of a million noise lines) and forced every commit to be staged
# by explicit path.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to normalise text files to LF in the repository, so a
# CRLF working file and an LF stored file are no longer a difference. `eol=lf`
# also checks them out as LF on every platform, so the two sides agree rather
# than converting back and forth.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Leave the actual binaries alone — normalising these would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
